 {"id":"fabro-d20f","title":"Planner briefs must quote the actual heading when correcting a seed's path citation","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T13:14:18.366Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T13:22:23.687Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 7, add: when a brief corrects a seed's path/heading citation, it must quote the actual heading text read from the target file (reading the section, not grepping the line). Expected effect: eliminates the false-correction class, saves 1-2 LLM rounds per affected run, stops contradictory briefs reaching review. Evidence: planner grepped journal/<run_id> in analyze.md, found fallback at line 48, asserted the seed's 'Step 3.5' wording wrong (seq 51-53, 66); the section IS headed 'Step 3.5' (line 44); reviewer proved it (seq 181-183). Closed fabro-cf76 (existence check) cannot catch this; closed fabro-c0a8 covers genuinely stale paths. Basis: run 01M23443Z65RK83WTF4Z7D7PGD, workflow version 6417aaf5473539a3e260007c8872e2b6ab6c63fbfe6f243acb03e4fcdd92424d, commit afcf8f157051d57ca8630f469a361d224679c4f9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-c0ca","title":"Planner briefs: specify insertion points as quoted anchor text, not absolute line numbers","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T13:46:35.895Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T13:52:33.405Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md steps 6-7, require briefs to name insertion points as quoted anchor text (e.g. insert after the line reading 'keep working through the shell.') instead of absolute line ranges, and drop the planner's anchor-locating greps (that is implementer work). Expected effect: -1 implementer verification round and -2 planner tool calls (~35s); eliminates the off-by-N insertion risk class at the source. Distinct from open fabro-d20f (quoting headings when correcting citations) and fabro-645d (implementer read discipline that assumes line anchors persist). Basis: run 01M235V6FWMNBDKS9BH3T25G2D, workflow version 78e816b2619802a23f8ddde5c31eb134267b0d6e9f40ddd161e8c50ff9a697a3, commit 5858b03b0d83e91d34e0425b25c53c9580e18a6c","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-8d81","title":"ml record: print the mx-id on success (upstream) and document an ml search recovery line in implementer.md","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T13:46:36.029Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T13:52:33.322Z","description":"Two-part change: (1) upstream mulch-cli (@os-eco/mulch-cli 0.10.7, pinned in the toolchain image) should print the mx-id on successful 'ml record' and pre-validate flags; (2) interim line in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md lesson-capture section: the success output prints no mx-id — recover it via 'ml search <domain>' without piping through head (which swallowed the first result). Expected effect: -3 tool calls / -2 LLM rounds (~25s, ~$0.015) on every lesson-capturing pass. Orthogonal to open fabro-96bd (flag contract docs) and fabro-b94d (domain auto-creation churn). Basis: run 01M235V6FWMNBDKS9BH3T25G2D, workflow version 78e816b2619802a23f8ddde5c31eb134267b0d6e9f40ddd161e8c50ff9a697a3, commit 5858b03b0d83e91d34e0425b25c53c9580e18a6c SCOPE 2026-09-09 (dispatch): @fabro implements part (2) only — the interim implementer.md recovery line. Part (1) (upstream mulch-cli change) waits for the user's upstream-posture decision; the line must NOT open upstream issues/PRs autonomously.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
+{"id":"fabro-7ac9","title":"Engine: per-seed fs_hide exception when the claimed brief targets only hidden paths","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T15:29:49.408Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T15:29:49.408Z","description":"In run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG the implementer's first read_file on `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` was denied by fs_hide (event seq 95), forcing all 10 seed-target edits through shell heredoc python3 scripts — the implementer stage consumed 86% of run cost and 84% of wall (15 of 19 min). Change the fs_hide resolution in `lib/components/fabro-workflow` so that when the claimed seed brief's target paths all fall inside the fs_hide list, file tools are allowed for those paths. Not covered by open fabro-d02d (denial message only) or fabro-8296 (glob notice). Expected effect: eliminates the discovery turn and error-prone heredoc-edit mode for every workflow-asset-targeting seed. Capability-affecting (ADR-0019): this changes agent file-tool permissions on hidden paths; fix direction is engine-mediated only (fs_hide resolution logic in `lib/components/fabro-workflow`, no new tools or raw clients); implementation awaits explicit user approval. Basis: run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG, workflow version 3bd915204178a8e5fd6796670d1bbfae4248a4b01f5d0fb7201e53b394cfdda8, commit db6b8ca5b4f7c0fc7583e1d28df1fa9ba295958e","labels":["needs-user","revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-8cef","title":"Evidence capture: emit the reviewer-facing blob as plain-text multi-line, not a JSON-escaped single line","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T15:29:49.582Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T15:29:49.582Z","description":"The evidence capture for run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG was 55,353 bytes as a single-line JSON-escaped string; read_file truncated mid-diff and the reviewer paged it with `nu str substring` in three calls before judging (reviewer journal painpoint, window at 3.1% of 1M — format, not size, forced the detour). Change `scripts/evidence.nu` to write the capture blob as plain-text multi-line so one read_file suffices. Budget-raise alternative (preamble 24→32, inline 16→32) dropped as duplicate of open fabro-35ab and fabro-3c9d. Expected effect: one read instead of three per review; removes substring-paging misparse risk and ~60–90s reviewer latency on asset-heavy seeds. Basis: run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG, workflow version 3bd915204178a8e5fd6796670d1bbfae4248a4b01f5d0fb7201e53b394cfdda8, commit db6b8ca5b4f7c0fc7583e1d28df1fa9ba295958e","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-607a","title":"Keep concrete literals at PROJECT_FACTS indirection sites","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T15:30:01.177Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T15:30:01.177Z","description":"After seed fabro-4814 externalized repo facts, planner.md step 4 now says \"shell grep for the seed id prefix (PROJECT_FACTS)\" where `fabro-` used to be inline — an LLM must resolve the indirection through the include to run the double-pick guard correctly (reviewer observation, non-blocking). Change `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` step 4 and the corresponding use sites in `prompts/project-facts.md` to carry the concrete example at each site (\"the seed id prefix (e.g. `fabro-`)\") and keep the table as the source of truth. Expected effect: removes a misparse class from the exact mechanism that prevents fabro-22e4-style double-picks; near-zero cost. Basis: run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG, workflow version 3bd915204178a8e5fd6796670d1bbfae4248a4b01f5d0fb7201e53b394cfdda8, commit db6b8ca5b4f7c0fc7583e1d28df1fa9ba295958e","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-9967","title":"Planner prompt: cap sd ready to a top-N view and pass created_since to fabro_runs_list","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T15:30:01.314Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T15:30:01.314Z","description":"Run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG seq 32: `sd ready --assignee fabro --limit 200` returned 189 issues / 25,613 bytes to pick one candidate; seq 41: `fabro_runs_list` returned 12,676 bytes / 14 runs where only status, PR state, and goal matter for the in-flight guard. Change the command table in `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` to use `--limit 10` for `sd ready` and pass a recency filter to `fabro_runs_list` (in-flight runs are recent by definition). Expected effect: ~35KB less context in the planner's early turns, faster first output, less tie-break distraction. Basis: run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG, workflow version 3bd915204178a8e5fd6796670d1bbfae4248a4b01f5d0fb7201e53b394cfdda8, commit db6b8ca5b4f7c0fc7583e1d28df1fa9ba295958e","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-b769","title":"Add a long-stage heartbeat notification for run visibility","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T15:30:01.376Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T15:30:01.376Z","description":"Slack notifications in `.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.toml` are configured only for run.completed/run.failed; in run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG the implementer ran 15 of the run's 19 minutes with no external signal and no operator hook to cancel (run settings, cost concentration). Change the notifications block to add a stage-level event or a \"stage exceeds N minutes\" heartbeat alongside the terminal events. Expected effect: mid-run visibility into single-stage cost concentration while intervention is still possible. Basis: run 01M23B02H3ZNND8AT2D3Y2S4SG, workflow version 3bd915204178a8e5fd6796670d1bbfae4248a4b01f5d0fb7201e53b394cfdda8, commit db6b8ca5b4f7c0fc7583e1d28df1fa9ba295958e","labels":["revision"]}
